{"recall":{"defs":[["Artificial neuron","Weighted sum plus bias passed through an activation."],["Perceptron","Single neuron with a threshold activation."],["Learning rate","Step size of weight updates."],["Linearly separable","Classes separable by a hyperplane."],["Connectionism","Intelligence from interconnected simple units."],["Epoch","One pass over the training examples."]],"formulas":["z=\\sum_{i=1}^nw_ix_i+b","\\hat y=\\begin{cases}1&z\\ge0\\\\0&z<0\\end{cases}","w_i\\leftarrow w_i+\\eta(t-\\hat y)x_i","h=\\mathbf w^T\\tilde{\\mathbf x}"],"takeaways":["Neuron: z = Σwᵢxᵢ + b, ŷ = f(z).","Perceptron = linear threshold classifier.","AND, OR, NOT via one perceptron each.","Learn by updating on mistakes; converges if separable.","XOR needs hidden layers."],"confused":[["{0,1} vs {−1,+1}","Equivalent conventions."],["Weights vs bias","Feature importance vs threshold shift."],["Perceptron vs logistic regression","Step vs sigmoid; mistakes-only vs every-example updates."],["Linearly separable vs learnable","Perceptron can learn only the former."]],"minute":"An artificial neuron, inspired by biological neurons with dendrites, soma, axon and synapses, computes a weighted sum of its inputs plus a bias and applies an activation function; its knowledge lives in the weights. Networks of such neurons in input, hidden and output layers learn by tuning weights. The perceptron (Rosenblatt, 1958) outputs 1 when the weighted sum is at least zero: a linear classifier. It can implement AND (−1, 0.75, 0.75), OR (−1, 2, 2) and NOT, learning weights by wᵢ ← wᵢ + η(t − ŷ)xᵢ on mistakes, and converges whenever the data are linearly separable. XOR is not, so it requires a multi-layer network."},"flashcards":[["Brain numbers","~10¹⁰ neurons, 10⁴–10⁵ connections each, ~1 ms switching"],["Neuron parts","Dendrites, soma, axon, synapses"],["Artificial neuron","$z=\\sum w_ix_i+b,\\ \\hat y=f(z)$"],["Key insight","Simplified abstraction of biological neurons"],["ANN layers","Input, hidden, output"],["Connectionism","Knowledge in connection weights; learning changes them"],["Perceptron","Rosenblatt 1958; ŷ = 1 if wᵀx + b ≥ 0"],["AND weights","w₀ = −1, w₁ = w₂ = 0.75"],["OR weights","w₀ = −1, w₁ = w₂ = 2"],["Learning rule","$w_i\\leftarrow w_i+\\eta(t-\\hat y)x_i$"],["Convergence theorem","Finite steps if linearly separable"],["NOT final weights","w₁ = −1, w₀ = 0"],["XOR","Not linearly separable; needs multiple layers"],["Linear separability","Split by an (n − 1)-D hyperplane"]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["h1"],"deep":["n2-brain"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h1"],"deep":["n2-bio"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["what","h2"],"deep":["n2-artificial"],"viz":["neuronCalc"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h2"],"deep":["n2-math"],"viz":["neuronCalc"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h3"],"deep":["n2-compare"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h4"],"deep":["n2-ann"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h4"],"deep":["n2-props"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h4"],"deep":["n2-when"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h5"],"deep":["n2-connect"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h5"],"deep":["n2-principles"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h6"],"deep":["n2-perceptron"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h7"],"deep":["n2-gates"],"viz":["gateLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h7"],"deep":["n2-and"],"viz":["gateLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h7"],"deep":["n2-or"],"viz":["gateLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h8","demo"],"deep":["n2-learn"],"viz":["perceptronStepper"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h9"],"deep":["n2-not"],"viz":["perceptronStepper"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h10"],"deep":["n2-xor"],"viz":["gateLab","perceptronStepper"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h10"],"deep":["n2-xorfail"],"viz":["perceptron2D"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h11"],"deep":["n2-linsep"],"viz":["perceptron2D"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h11"],"deep":["n2-pls"],"viz"